<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barcid family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Barcid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barcid family was a leading Carthaginian family of the third century BCE, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca">Hamilcar Barca</a> and his sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, Hasdrubal and Mago. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a> they built a power base in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines. Hannibal's invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from there began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, whose defeat brought the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barcid-family.jpg" alt="Barcid family" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Ogre at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hasdrubal_coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
